.SH "NAME"
.PP
xgate \- gate daemon: SSH bastion with session recording and SFTP mediation
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBxgate\fR [\fB\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-validate\fR] [\fB\-version\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBxgate\fR is the gate: the daemon people log into. It reads one YAML configuration file (see \fBxproxy.yaml\fR(5)), binds the listeners it describes or takes them from systemd socket activation, and serves until stopped.
.PP
It serves the listener kinds of the gate role, which today is \fBssh\fR: the bastion, its per\-principal policy, its SFTP mediation and its session recording. A session belongs to a named principal, is recorded to an asciicast file, can be made to carry a second factor, and is bounded by a policy written in SSH\(aqs own terms \[u2014] which channels, requests, subsystems, commands, environment variables and forwards are allowed \[u2014] rather than by a destination list.
.PP
The internet\-facing HTTP machinery its sibling \fBxproxy\fR(8) runs is a separate program and a separate process with a separate user. A listener of another role in the same file is validated in full and left to its owner, which is what lets the three share a set of includes; a listener kind this binary did not link is never bound.
.PP
The process runs as the \fBxgate\fR user under the shipped systemd unit and confines itself with Landlock, seccomp and a dropped capability set (see \fBdocs/HARDENING.md\fR). It is controlled at run time through its own management socket by \fBxproxyctl\fR(8).
